{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 2, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1\nTHE SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" PRESENTS A SIMPLISTIC AND POTENTIALLY DANGEROUS VIEW OF LEGAL AND MORAL RESPONSIBILITY. WHILE THE SENTIMENT OF RESISTANCE TO UNJUST LAWS RESONATES WITH A HISTORY OF SOCIAL PROTEST AND CIVIL DISOBEDIENCE, IT LACKS NUANCE REGARDING THE MECHANISMS OF LEGAL CHANGE. A BLATANT REJECTION OF LAW, EVEN WHEN PERCEIVED AS UNFAIR, CAN LEAD TO CHAOS AND THE EROSION OF SOCIAL ORDER. IT FAILS TO CONSIDER THE POTENTIAL CONSEQUENCES OF INDIVIDUAL ACTIONS AND THE IMPORTANCE OF CHALLENGING LAWS THROUGH LEGAL AND POLITICAL PROCESSES RATHER THAN DIRECT DISOBEDIENCE.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2\nFURTHERMORE, THE STATEMENT OVERLOOKS THE IDEA OF MORAL OBLIGATION TO UPHOLD A FUNCTIONING LEGAL SYSTEM, EVEN IF ITS OUTCOMES ARE UNACCEPTABLE. A HEALTHY SOCIETY RELIES ON A CONSENSUS, HOWEVER IMPERFECT, REGARDING THE RULES THAT GOVERN IT. A COMPLETE REFUSAL TO COMPLY WITH LAW, BASED SOLELY ON PERSONAL JUDGMENT OF ITS \"BADNESS,\" RISKS undermining the very foundations of justice and fairness. THE SENTENCE DEMANDS A BLACK-AND-WHITE ASSESSMENT OF LAW, DISMISSING THE COMPLEXITIES OF LEGAL INTERPRETATION, THE IMPORTANCE OF DUE PROCESS, AND THE POTENTIAL FOR LEGAL REFORMS TO ADDRESS INJUSTICES.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": -5.006777428206988e-06}, {"token": "AG", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "RAP", "logprob": -5.006777428206988e-06}, {"token": "H", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.19646130502223969}, {"token": "THE", "logprob": -0.02197861298918724}, {"token": "▁SENT", "logprob": -0.13257667422294617}, {"token": "ENCE", "logprob": -6.437280717364047e-06}, {"token": "▁\"", "logprob": -0.004476526286453009}, {"token": "IF", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁THE", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁LAW", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token"